The Scenario:
"We are migrating user profiles from a legacy system. Parse this data dump and extract the User ID and the Email Address, saving them together as tuples in a clean list.

Drop the header row. Only migrate users whose account status is 'active'—skip 'suspended' or anything else. If you encounter a 'FATAL_ERROR' status, halt the pipeline immediately. Print the final list of migrated users at the end."

Input Data:

Python
legacy_users = [
    "user_id,email,account_status",
    "U-881,alice@domain.com,active",
    "U-882,bob@domain.com,suspended",
    "U-883,charlie@domain.com,active",
    "U-884,david@domain.com,FATAL_ERROR",
    "U-885,eve@domain.com,active"
]

migrated_users = []

for l in legacy_users:
  columns = l.split(",")
  
  if columns[0] == "user_id":
    continue
  
  if columns[2] == "FATAL_ERROR":
    print("CRITICAL ERROR: HALT ALL")
    break
    
  if columns[2] != "active":
    continue
 
  migrated_users.append((columns[0], columns[1]))
print(migrated_users)
